{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 14,
      "name": "Rolling Blobs",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "The fun is in tuning ball speed, spacing and size against a 16 stud/s runner, so each layout needs a hand check that a safe line always exists. There are few clean knobs, so a generator would mostly make unfair or boring mixes.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "ball shape and the see-through \"blob\" look (GooDrops already uses 4-stud blob balls)",
          "slide motion (back-and-forth along one axis, timed from server time with a phase)",
          "side bays next to a narrow path (GooWave builds these)",
          "climbing sections with rise; plain slabs for walls, pockets and steps"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "\"travel\" motion: built on Goo Rides' (idea 3) ride motion, a path of points, but one-way with no stops: the ball runs the path once per period, then pops back to the launcher. Several balls share one path with phase offsets, all timed from server time so every player sees the same balls",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "ball firing order from Crusher Alley's (idea 1) 'pattern' motion: a list of beats per launcher (fire, skip, big ball, small ball) instead of one even beat, for Burst and Lull, Big and Small and Odd One Out",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "rolling look: the ball spins to match its speed and squashes a little where it lands",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "bounce option on travel: the ball hops in arcs of a set height between landing points",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "ramps: reuse Ice Slide's (idea 6) 'slope pieces' (a tilted slab placed at an angle), in plain floor material, so balls and players go up and down a real slope",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "launcher at the top: a pipe mouth that shows the next ball sitting in it (its real size and lane), glows and rumbles 1 s before it lets go",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "hazard touch = back to the start pad and the red half-transparent hazard look: shared with every hazard idea (named in Crusher Alley, idea 1); balls only need to use it",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "Red see-through balls with a low rumble, always coming out of a launcher you can see, and the next ball waits glowing in its mouth at its real size. Small balls (3 studs) are low enough to jump; big balls (6 studs and up) are clearly too tall, so you step aside. A ball always rolls or hops along a path; nothing in this idea stands still or swings.",
      "generator": null,
